1
00:00:01,267 --> 00:00:06,107
♪ In the not-too-distant
future--next Sunday, A.D.-- ♪

2
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:08,677
♪ There was a guy named Joel ♪

3
00:00:08,710 --> 00:00:11,780
♪ Not too different
from you or me ♪

4
00:00:11,813 --> 00:00:15,383
♪ He worked
at Gizmonic Institute ♪

5
00:00:15,417 --> 00:00:18,487
♪ Just another face
in a red jumpsuit ♪

6
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:21,488
♪ He did a good job cleaning up
the place, ♪

7
00:00:21,522 --> 00:00:23,257
♪ But his bosses
didn't like him ♪

8
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:27,462
♪ So they shot him into space ♪

9
00:00:27,495 --> 00:00:30,632
♪ We'll send him cheesy movies ♪

10
00:00:30,665 --> 00:00:32,400
♪ The worst we can find ♪

11
00:00:32,433 --> 00:00:34,102
♪ La-la-la ♪

12
00:00:34,135 --> 00:00:36,805
♪ He'll have to sit
and watch them all ♪

13
00:00:36,838 --> 00:00:40,142
♪ Then we'll monitor his mind ♪

14
00:00:40,175 --> 00:00:42,743
♪ Now keep in mind
Joel can't control ♪

15
00:00:42,777 --> 00:00:46,347
♪ When the movies begin or end ♪

16
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:49,150
♪ Because he used
those special parts ♪

17
00:00:49,183 --> 00:00:54,155
♪ To make his robot friends ♪

18
00:00:54,188 --> 00:00:55,623
♪ Robot roll-call-- ♪

19
00:00:55,657 --> 00:00:57,258
♪ Cambot ♪

20
00:00:57,292 --> 00:00:58,392
♪ Gypsy ♪

21
00:00:58,425 --> 00:01:00,162
♪ Tom Servo ♪

22
00:01:00,195 --> 00:01:01,595
♪ Crow ♪

23
00:01:01,628 --> 00:01:04,565
♪ If you're wondering
how he eats and breathes ♪

24
00:01:04,598 --> 00:01:06,868
♪ And other science facts ♪

25
00:01:06,902 --> 00:01:09,170
- ♪ La-la-la ♪
- ♪ Then repeat to yourself ♪

26
00:01:09,203 --> 00:01:13,575
♪ "It's just a show,
I should really just relax ♪

27
00:01:13,608 --> 00:01:19,247
♪ For Mystery Science
Theater 3000." ♪

28
00:01:29,423 --> 00:01:32,593
- Ohh.
- 30 seconds to commercial sign.

29
00:01:32,627 --> 00:01:35,230
- Morning, Crow.
- I'm Servo.

30
00:01:35,263 --> 00:01:37,165
- I mean Tom Servo.
- Morning.

31
00:01:37,198 --> 00:01:39,233
- Hey, good morning
breakfast clubbers.

32
00:01:39,267 --> 00:01:41,202
Heh, hey. How you doing?

33
00:01:41,235 --> 00:01:42,803
Hey, here's a little
morning poem.

34
00:01:42,837 --> 00:01:44,605
Birdie with a yellow bill

35
00:01:44,638 --> 00:01:45,873
Hopped upon my window sill

36
00:01:45,907 --> 00:01:48,242
Cocked his shining eye and said

37
00:01:48,275 --> 00:01:49,877
What's for breakfast, Grandma?

38
00:01:49,910 --> 00:01:53,447
- Oh, I hate morning bots.

39
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:54,482
- Ugh.

40
00:01:54,515 --> 00:01:57,485
- Commercial sign in 15 seconds.

41
00:01:57,518 --> 00:01:59,520
- That reminds me.
My name is Joel.

42
00:01:59,553 --> 00:02:02,657
And I'm the subject of a bizarre
movie watching experiment.

43
00:02:02,690 --> 00:02:03,892
And now I guess so are you.

44
00:02:03,925 --> 00:02:05,025
We're expecting a call
any minute

45
00:02:05,058 --> 00:02:07,762
from the quasi-evil overlords
who shot me into space.

46
00:02:07,795 --> 00:02:09,363
So stick around.

47
00:02:09,397 --> 00:02:12,200
- Yeah, if Crow's chipperness
doesn't kill us first.

48
00:02:12,233 --> 00:02:13,467
- Hey!

49
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:17,172
- Commercial sign in five,
four, three, two--

50
00:02:17,205 --> 00:02:18,238
commercial sign now.

51
00:02:18,272 --> 00:02:19,773
- Keep your head up, guys.

52
00:02:19,807 --> 00:02:22,677
- Stick around.
We'll be right back.

53
00:02:28,348 --> 00:02:31,785
All right. And...

54
00:02:31,818 --> 00:02:34,822
- There's the lady.
- Okay. I'm busted.

55
00:02:34,855 --> 00:02:37,692
All right, double or nothing.
Okay. Little game of chance.

56
00:02:37,725 --> 00:02:39,560
- Find the--
- There.

57
00:02:39,593 --> 00:02:43,263
- They're calling.
Come in, sirs.

58
00:02:43,297 --> 00:02:47,568
- Come in, Joel, my little 3.98
all-you-can-eat space buffet.

59
00:02:49,303 --> 00:02:50,805
- Hey, sirs, what's up?

60
00:02:50,838 --> 00:02:53,575
- Hey, sirs, what's up?
You know what's up.

61
00:02:53,608 --> 00:02:55,943
Make with the invention
exchange, pasty boy.

62
00:02:55,977 --> 00:02:57,445
- Hey, sirs, I'm ready.
Hey, Cambot,

63
00:02:57,478 --> 00:02:58,612
bring it in a little bit.

64
00:02:58,645 --> 00:03:01,515
This is a thing I invented
for people who are studying

65
00:03:01,548 --> 00:03:03,483
to be cartoon characters,
you know,

66
00:03:03,517 --> 00:03:05,953
It's like when a beautiful woman
comes by you in the cartoons,

67
00:03:05,987 --> 00:03:08,255
you go like this.

68
00:03:08,288 --> 00:03:10,692
Or like this.
Kind of like that.

69
00:03:10,725 --> 00:03:12,660
And then you get into
your upper level courses.

70
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:15,697
And you can do the walk by.

71
00:03:15,730 --> 00:03:19,233
She's great.
And then followed by.

72
00:03:19,267 --> 00:03:21,835
See. What do you think?

73
00:03:21,868 --> 00:03:24,438
- Not bad, not bad.

74
00:03:24,472 --> 00:03:26,373
- Now, get an eyeful
of our little wonder.

75
00:03:26,407 --> 00:03:28,442
- Yes, we've been dealing
with genetic mutations

76
00:03:28,475 --> 00:03:29,843
since you were in short pants.

77
00:03:29,877 --> 00:03:32,447
- And we finally applied
our principles to carnival food.

78
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:34,948
We came up with cotton candy
that scream when you bite it.

79
00:03:34,982 --> 00:03:36,817
- May I?
- Enjoy.

80
00:03:36,850 --> 00:03:40,855
- Ow! That's my head! Ow!

81
00:03:40,888 --> 00:03:44,392
- Well, what do you think of
that, Joel-arini?

82
00:03:44,425 --> 00:03:47,295
- You're toying with God's
blueprint, that's what I think.

83
00:03:47,328 --> 00:03:48,395
- Yeah!

84
00:03:48,428 --> 00:03:49,662
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

85
00:03:49,695 --> 00:03:53,768
- Well, Joel, we've got another
cinematic compost pile for you

86
00:03:53,802 --> 00:03:55,603
called The Slime People.

87
00:03:55,637 --> 00:03:59,007
- Oh, it's scabby and bumpy
and absolutely hideous.

88
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:01,042
- But first,
another space frolic

89
00:04:01,075 --> 00:04:03,610
with our bullet-headed friend,
Commando Cody.

90
00:04:03,643 --> 00:04:05,278
- Enjoy.

91
00:04:05,312 --> 00:04:08,248
[Buzzing, Screaming]

92
00:04:23,732 --> 00:04:25,065
- You know, I just don't think

93
00:04:25,098 --> 00:04:27,868
that cotton candy thing
was legitimate.

94
00:04:27,902 --> 00:04:30,405
- I don't know.
It look pretty real.

95
00:04:33,842 --> 00:04:36,043
- A new character--Commando Cody

96
00:04:36,077 --> 00:04:39,847
in Radar Men from the Moon.

97
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:42,883
[Music plays]

98
00:04:51,692 --> 00:04:54,662
- It is sort of hypnotic,
isn't it?

99
00:04:54,695 --> 00:04:57,898
- Hip, not ick.

100
00:05:02,570 --> 00:05:05,573
[Humming to music]

101
00:05:15,717 --> 00:05:19,853
- I wish the scientists would
install one of those oil things.

102
00:05:19,887 --> 00:05:22,057
- Oh, the oil and water things?

103
00:05:28,695 --> 00:05:30,465
- Hills of Death.

104
00:05:31,765 --> 00:05:34,368
The production company has
installed a small piece

105
00:05:34,402 --> 00:05:36,870
of information for you
the readers to read

106
00:05:36,903 --> 00:05:39,840
as if you cared about what
happened in the last segment.

107
00:05:42,743 --> 00:05:44,912
♪ Something new is coming
to town ♪

108
00:05:44,945 --> 00:05:47,013
♪ And George the milkman
is bringing it 'round ♪

109
00:05:48,817 --> 00:05:50,485
- You think we'll meet them
on the road?

110
00:05:50,518 --> 00:05:53,387
- Of course you will.
You did last week.

111
00:05:56,957 --> 00:05:58,492
- Truck.

112
00:06:04,198 --> 00:06:05,600
- Car.

113
00:06:05,633 --> 00:06:08,002
- If I remember right.
Cody's about to collide

114
00:06:08,035 --> 00:06:11,638
with the evil Good Humor Man's
ice cream car of death.

115
00:06:11,672 --> 00:06:13,640
- Bet you an ROKP they jump.

116
00:06:15,442 --> 00:06:18,045
- There it is.

117
00:06:20,582 --> 00:06:22,082
- It's going to crash into us!

118
00:06:22,115 --> 00:06:23,918
- Bail out!

119
00:06:27,555 --> 00:06:30,792
- Oh, did I say jump?
I meant swerve.

120
00:06:33,193 --> 00:06:35,863
- Oh, great,
that was on my MasterCard.

121
00:06:43,103 --> 00:06:44,705
- Here's the payroll.

122
00:06:44,738 --> 00:06:47,642
- I said jelly rolls
not payrolls.

123
00:06:47,675 --> 00:06:49,610
- Doh!

124
00:06:51,812 --> 00:06:52,947
- Retik calling Croft.

125
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:55,182
- Uh, Mr. Retik,
line one, please.

126
00:06:58,118 --> 00:07:02,088
- The donuts are here, sir.
They're fluffy and delicious.

127
00:07:02,122 --> 00:07:04,792
- I was just about to call you
to report that we are about

128
00:07:04,825 --> 00:07:06,893
to put our ray gun
into operation again.

129
00:07:06,927 --> 00:07:09,563
- I have another mission
for you first.

130
00:07:09,597 --> 00:07:12,233
Do you have an atomic bomb
strong enough

131
00:07:12,267 --> 00:07:15,870
to start a volcanic eruption
in the Mt. Alta crater?

132
00:07:15,903 --> 00:07:18,138
- Not on me.
- ...in that mountainous area

133
00:07:18,172 --> 00:07:19,272
would do very little damage.

134
00:07:19,305 --> 00:07:22,743
- On the contrary, it will do
a great deal of damage.

135
00:07:22,777 --> 00:07:25,112
The present atmospheric
conditions on earth

136
00:07:25,145 --> 00:07:28,582
indicate that the eruption would
cause torrential rains.

137
00:07:28,615 --> 00:07:32,085
And the resulting flood should
seriously disrupt transportation

138
00:07:32,118 --> 00:07:33,185
and defense measures.

139
00:07:33,218 --> 00:07:36,090
- An excellent idea.
We shall carry it out at once.

140
00:07:36,123 --> 00:07:37,257
- That's why he's the boss.

141
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:39,993
- Then start an intensified
campaign with the ray gun.

142
00:07:40,027 --> 00:07:43,097
Earth's defenses must be
completely broken down

143
00:07:43,130 --> 00:07:45,533
before we can risk
an invasion from the moon.

144
00:07:45,567 --> 00:07:46,833
Yes, your Excellency.

145
00:07:46,867 --> 00:07:48,035
- What a wing nut.

146
00:07:48,068 --> 00:07:51,705
- Oh, man you guys are gonna
love this one.

147
00:07:51,738 --> 00:07:53,640
- You heard the orders.

148
00:07:53,673 --> 00:07:56,143
Charter a plane and drop
one of our atomic bombs

149
00:07:56,177 --> 00:07:57,277
into the Alta crater.

150
00:07:57,310 --> 00:08:00,748
- Nature will do the rest.
- Okay. When do we do it?

151
00:08:00,782 --> 00:08:04,018
- At once.
I will get you the bomb.

152
00:08:04,052 --> 00:08:07,488
- It's right over here
by the toaster oven.

153
00:08:12,025 --> 00:08:14,562
- This one's called
"The Baby Boy."

154
00:08:17,598 --> 00:08:19,867
- Joel, what's the matter
with these guys anyway?

155
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:22,202
I mean, they're ready
to sell their home planet

156
00:08:22,235 --> 00:08:23,402
for some money.

157
00:08:23,435 --> 00:08:27,608
- Well, they just don't have
any real home planet pride.

158
00:08:27,642 --> 00:08:29,677
- You think they have wives
and families?

159
00:08:29,710 --> 00:08:30,910
- Yeah.

160
00:08:30,943 --> 00:08:34,082
- No, I bet they sold them too
to pay for those nice suits.

161
00:08:34,115 --> 00:08:37,285
- You know, the Cessna Skyhawk
is usually your best choice

162
00:08:37,318 --> 00:08:39,120
for bombardiering missions.

163
00:08:39,153 --> 00:08:41,188
- Here it goes.

164
00:08:43,290 --> 00:08:45,927
- Good shot.
Right in the wading pool.

165
00:08:54,068 --> 00:08:56,637
Krakatoa east of Java.

166
00:08:56,670 --> 00:08:58,973
Bentonville east of Monsey.

167
00:09:00,975 --> 00:09:04,545
Competition keen as nation's
best vie for top honors.

168
00:09:11,018 --> 00:09:14,322
- Hey, you ho-daddys. Surf's up.

169
00:09:14,355 --> 00:09:16,257
- Oops, the water broke.

170
00:09:22,028 --> 00:09:23,297
- That's a bridge under
troubled water.

171
00:09:23,330 --> 00:09:26,100
- They'll be surfing in Boston.

172
00:09:35,175 --> 00:09:37,778
- Local high school
grabs corn crown.

173
00:09:37,812 --> 00:09:39,947
Bluerth to build beet palace.

174
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:42,215
- If the moon men did start
that eruption,

175
00:09:42,248 --> 00:09:44,085
they certainly got results.

176
00:09:44,118 --> 00:09:46,220
- You've got to admire
them moon men.

177
00:09:46,253 --> 00:09:48,055
- That volcano's been dead
for years.

178
00:09:48,088 --> 00:09:49,990
Took quite a blast
to get it going again.

179
00:09:50,023 --> 00:09:52,058
An atomic bomb dropped
from a plane

180
00:09:52,092 --> 00:09:53,293
would seem to be
the only answer.

181
00:09:53,327 --> 00:09:56,663
- He's right for $200.

182
00:09:56,697 --> 00:10:00,768
- Oh, finally I come in and you
two aren't fighting anybody.

183
00:10:00,802 --> 00:10:03,137
- How'd you make out?
- Like a bandit.

184
00:10:03,170 --> 00:10:05,673
- The second airport I checked
had chartered a plane

185
00:10:05,707 --> 00:10:07,240
on the day of the eruption
to two men,

186
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:09,677
answering to the description
of Graber and his pal.

187
00:10:09,710 --> 00:10:11,812
- Then we're right. They're
the ones who bombed the volcano.

188
00:10:11,845 --> 00:10:12,778
- Looks like it.

189
00:10:12,812 --> 00:10:14,315
- Yes, but that doesn't help us
catch them.

190
00:10:14,348 --> 00:10:15,348
Couldn't you get a line on them?

191
00:10:15,382 --> 00:10:17,250
- The names and addresses
they gave are phony.

192
00:10:17,283 --> 00:10:18,852
But I did get one break.

193
00:10:18,885 --> 00:10:20,988
The airport manager borrowed
these matches from Graber

194
00:10:21,022 --> 00:10:22,188
and forgot to get them back.

195
00:10:22,222 --> 00:10:24,725
- Al's Cafe.
That might do us some good.

196
00:10:24,758 --> 00:10:26,260
- Especially if you're hungry.

197
00:10:26,293 --> 00:10:28,228
- And if we're lucky,
they might be regular customers.

198
00:10:28,262 --> 00:10:29,863
So let's go
and look the joint over.

199
00:10:29,897 --> 00:10:30,963
- Right.

200
00:10:30,997 --> 00:10:33,167
- Crooks are always dropping
obvious clues like that.

201
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:36,803
It's really a desperate cry
for help, you know.

202
00:10:36,837 --> 00:10:40,307
- Oh, Al's Cafe,
they do a really nice job there.

203
00:10:40,340 --> 00:10:41,808
Blue plate special
that'll really make

204
00:10:41,842 --> 00:10:43,277
your pelt stand on end.

205
00:10:43,310 --> 00:10:45,813
- ...but I don't know their
names or anything about 'em.

206
00:10:45,847 --> 00:10:47,415
- Well, if they show up,
I wish you'd call me.

207
00:10:47,448 --> 00:10:49,117
- Sure,
I've got nothing better to do

208
00:10:49,150 --> 00:10:50,852
with my miserable life
than call you.

209
00:10:50,885 --> 00:10:52,787
- I sure will, Mr. Cody.
- Thanks.

210
00:10:56,057 --> 00:11:00,193
- Hey, how convenient.
Everybody dance!

211
00:11:00,227 --> 00:11:01,928
- They're all short order
crooks.

212
00:11:04,465 --> 00:11:08,935
- Uh, gentlemen,
I can seat you immediately.

213
00:11:10,470 --> 00:11:12,807
- You know, dropping those
matchbooks all over town

214
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:14,708
really helped business.

215
00:11:14,742 --> 00:11:16,877
- Well, this is my lucky day.

216
00:11:21,482 --> 00:11:23,250
- He'd like that to go.

217
00:11:25,352 --> 00:11:27,053
- Right in the kidney beans.

218
00:11:27,087 --> 00:11:29,123
- Right in the cream corn.

219
00:11:29,157 --> 00:11:30,190
- Right in the liver and onions.

220
00:11:30,223 --> 00:11:32,158
- Right in the Salisbury steak.

221
00:11:42,135 --> 00:11:44,138
- That's it. Next time I talk,

222
00:11:44,172 --> 00:11:47,173
I let this
do the talking for me.

223
00:11:47,207 --> 00:11:49,477
- You or the cops try to follow
us, I'll give it to him quick.

224
00:11:49,510 --> 00:11:51,812
- Give what?

225
00:11:51,845 --> 00:11:56,250
- The bill.
- Oh, put that on my tab.

226
00:12:01,022 --> 00:12:03,257
- Hey, isn't anyone going
to drive?

227
00:12:09,930 --> 00:12:11,965
- All right, Ted, we're going
to Barney's Chili Snack

228
00:12:11,998 --> 00:12:13,500
and do the same thing.

229
00:12:13,533 --> 00:12:17,403
- Wake up, Cody.
You owe me $400.

230
00:12:17,437 --> 00:12:21,108
- Cough up.
- They took your pal, Mr. Cody.

231
00:12:21,142 --> 00:12:24,178
- You gonna call the cops?
- I don't dare to.

232
00:12:24,212 --> 00:12:26,147
They'd kill him sure.

233
00:12:29,082 --> 00:12:30,885
- Oh, I'm stuffed.

234
00:12:30,918 --> 00:12:33,153
That's the best progressive
dinner I've ever had.

235
00:12:33,187 --> 00:12:35,823
Martha's Jell-O mold
was out of this world.

236
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:42,863
- Get your hand off my knee.

237
00:12:49,470 --> 00:12:51,038
- Huh?

238
00:12:57,945 --> 00:13:00,080
- Good reaction time.

239
00:13:00,113 --> 00:13:02,483
- Hey, give them a break.
They're trashed.

240
00:13:04,885 --> 00:13:07,353
- Come and get me.
I'm a fuzzy little fuzzy rabbit.

241
00:13:07,387 --> 00:13:10,057
I'm being bad.
You have to spank me.

242
00:13:10,090 --> 00:13:12,392
I've been bad, bad, bad, bad.

243
00:13:12,425 --> 00:13:13,560
- Soon as he can get to a phone,

244
00:13:13,593 --> 00:13:15,028
he'll have the cops
on our trail.

245
00:13:15,062 --> 00:13:16,062
- The bunny trail.

246
00:13:16,095 --> 00:13:18,498
- The road to Clark Mountain
is just up ahead.

247
00:13:18,532 --> 00:13:21,468
We'll hide out there until
Qua can send us another car.

248
00:13:24,605 --> 00:13:27,373
- Come back,
the bunny's still in the bushes.

249
